    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0429" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg321"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lincoln to Mr.
                            Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-03-03"><hi rendition="#italic">March 3, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 931.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to Mr. Foster’s dispatch No.
                    1053, of the 8th ultimo, regarding British pretensions with reference to the
                    Mosquito Reservation in Nicaragua, I have the honor to acquaint you that on the
                    1st instant I called upon Lord Rosebery at the foreign office and communicated
                    the above-mentioned dispatch to his lordship by reading it to him and, at his
                    request, leaving a copy with him.</p>
                <p>His lordship did not go into the subject further than to say that it would have
                    his attention at once.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert T.
                    Lincoln.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
